    {
      "id": "dmymib2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "INTRODUCTION TO ECONOMIC PLANNING"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Economic planning in India was initiated to guide resource allocation, growth, and social justice.",
        "The First Five-Year Plan (1951–1956) prioritized agricultural growth and development.",
        "A Plan Holiday was declared between 1966 and 1969 due to economic instability and war.",
        "The 12th Five-Year Plan (2012–2017) was the final Five-Year Plan in India.",
        "NITI Aayog replaced the Planning Commission in 2015 to foster cooperative federalism."
      ],
      "id": "xd0ycbe"
    },
